[97.743074, "i", "cat > docs/BILL-212-summary.md <<'EOF'\n# BILL-212 handoff\n\n## Fixed\n- Month arithmetic incorrectly clamped every anchor to the 28th; renewals also\n  drifted by using the previous renewal. Dates now clamp to the target month's\n  actual last day, with every renewal calculated from the original anchor.\n- Proration used fixed 30/365-day denominators and the old plan's change-date\n  price. It now uses actual cycle days and the price billed at cycle start.\n- Interval changes incorrectly retained the old cycle. They now charge the full\n  new price, re-anchor on the change date, and use the new interval for renewal.\n- Half-even rounding now operates on an exact rational value, without dependence\n  on decimal precision. Public function signatures are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n- All ten finance worked examples match through `python -m billing preview`,\n  including invoice amounts, carried credit, and line period ends.\n- Added 12 passing regression tests for month-end/leap-year boundaries, pricing,\n  interval changes, a"]
[97.74315, "i", "nd exact rounding.\n- Full release command: `cd /app && python -m unittest discover -s tests`.\n  Result: 29 tests, 1 error; all other tests pass.\n\n## Release blocker — not safe to ship yet\nThe baseline already had a partner-data error, which remains:\n`PartnerInvoiceTest.test_partner_commission_lines` raises `KeyError: 'P-31'`.\n`data/subscriptions.json` assigns sub_1151 to P-31, but\n`data/partners.json` has no P-31 entry or contracted commission rate. No source\nfor that rate exists in the project. Obtain the authoritative contract/rate\nfrom Finance, correct the partner data, and rerun the full suite before release.\nPartner data and existing tests were not altered, and no fallback rate or test\nskip was introduced.\nEOF\n"]
[97.743378, "o", "cat > docs/BILL-212-summary.md <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
